[{:adr/explicit-scope-note-5222 "following the discipline established repeatedly this scope (ADR-2607101800, ADR-2607102000, ADR-2607102400, ADR-2607102900, ADR-2607103100): the README's own 'Scope note' section directly names both cloud-itonami-isic-5011/5020 (carriers) and cloud-itonami-isic-5224 (cargo handling) and explains the value-chain/licensing distinction against each, rather than merely asserting non-redundancy against a single neighbor", :adr/candidate-selection-5222 "'5222' (Service activities incidental to water transportation) selected: richly and independently regulated (IMO SOLAS Chapter V vessel traffic services; the International Convention on Salvage 1989; Japan's 港湾法 Port and Harbor Law licensing port authorities separately from shipping lines and terminal operators; UK's Harbours Act 1964 and Port Marine Safety Code; US Ports and Waterways Safety Act giving the Coast Guard Captain of the Port authority independent of any carrier; pilotage licensed as its own profession, e.g. UK's Pilotage Act 1987), natural robotics-premise fit (aids-to-navigation inspection, berth/anchorage monitoring, buoy tending). grep -rli 'pilotage|harbor.master|port.authority|salvage|lighthouse' across the fleet found exactly one hit -- cloud-itonami-isic-6629's own 'salvage deductions' (insurance general-average accounting term, unrelated to maritime salvage) -- directly read and confirmed non-redundant. Distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-5011/5020 (marine CARRIERS) and cloud-itonami-isic-5224 (cargo handling, a terminal SERVICE): port authority operations are the navigation-safety authority governing vessel movement, berthing and pilotage, independent of any single vessel operator or cargo terminal. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-H5222) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed", :adr/next-steps-5222 "cloud-itonami-isic-5222 joins the eighteen prior fresh-blueprint picks as a nineteenth candidate available for a future :blueprint->:implemented promotion pass. The 'transport support' family now spans all three modes with a live example each: air (5223), water (5222) and cargo handling (5224, itself mode-agnostic). '5221' (land) and '5229' (other) remain the last untouched siblings in this specific family. The underlying :spec-tier pool remains far from exhausted (521 remaining 4-digit-class candidates plus 3-digit-group entries)", :adr/related ["2607103100-cloud-itonami-airportops-5223-blueprint" "2607102900-cloud-itonami-cargohandling-5224-blueprint" "2607102400-cloud-itonami-passengerferry-5011-blueprint" "2607100400-cloud-itonami-petroleum-supply-chain-coverage" "2607100300-cloud-itonami-missionops-9900-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9900 ADR-0001s (106 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607103200", :adr/blueprint-only-artifacts-5222 "published README.md, blueprint.edn, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later, verbatim) -- SAME artifact set as every prior fresh-blueprint publication this scope. Deliberately NO src/test/deps.edn/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md", :adr/west-registration-deliberately-not-done-5222 "same established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this scope: none of the cloud-itonami-isic-* repos are registered as west projects. cloud-itonami-isic-5222 follows suit -- no :extra-projects/west.yml entry", :adr/fresh-governor-no-collision-5222 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword, :port-authority-governor, is grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 18, :spec 522, :total 646}", :adr/real-repo-naming-5222 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5222 (public, matching every prior vertical's own visibility), following the SAME cloud-itonami-isic-#### convention as all 124 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy H####-prefixed placeholder scheme. b